<!-- 16 · deploy it -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="head"><span><b>Deploy it</b></span><span>16</span></div>
  <div class="kicker">Events happen every week</div>
  <h2 style="font-size:64px">Run it for your event, with our team, under your terms.</h2>
  <div class="cols c3" style="margin-top:50px">
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">01 · FOR OTHER EVENTS</div><h3>The platform, customised</h3><p>Most events do not manage their data well before, during or after. The same platform, cut to each one; the customer pays for what they use.</p></div>
    <div class="card g"><div class="n">02 · AS THE TEAM</div><h3>The agentic team, deployed</h3><p>The team that runs this newsroom, for a project, an event or a body of content: its roles, written limits, budgets and record come with it.</p></div>
    <div class="card r"><div class="n">03 · UNDER LICENCE</div><h3>On a company's own terms</h3><p>Our technology licensed to a company on its own terms, and maintained by us.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="vs" style="margin-top:46px;grid-template-columns:1fr 90px 1fr">
    <div class="side old" style="padding:30px 36px"><h3 style="font-size:32px;margin-bottom:12px">Open, for everyone</h3><p class="body" style="font-size:24px">Code Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0. Read it, fork it, run it.</p></div>
    <div class="mid">+</div>
    <div class="side new" style="padding:30px 36px"><h3 style="font-size:32px;margin-bottom:12px">Licensed, for a company</h3><p class="body" style="font-size:24px">Its own terms, its own version, maintained by the people who built it.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src" style="margin-top:26px">Dual licensing (Dinis Cruz, 7 Nov 2026); open-source.sgit.ai/practice: "You can always commercial-license or relicense everything for a customer who wants it".</div>
  <div class="foot"><span class="wordmark">Promp<span class="t">T</span><span class="u">ugal</span><i>.news</i></span><span>The platform</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 17 · in numbers -->
<section class="slide">
